<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44338" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐϋκτίμενος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῐ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			ʽκτίζὠ</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ ναιόμενος</span>
			, <i>good to dwell in</i>, epith. of cities, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐϋ. πτολίεθρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.501
				</span></i>
			, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					5.149
				</span></i>
			; of anything on which man's labour has been bestowed,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῆσον ἐϋκτιμένην ἐκάμοντο</span>
			wrought it <i>so as to be good to dwell in</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.130
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐϋ. ἐν ἀλωῇ</span> on a
				<i>well-made</i> threshing-floor, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				20.496
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				21.77
			</span></i>; the same phrase, of a garden, <i>well-wrought</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				24.226
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐκτ</span>- in <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				36
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
			</span></i> l.c.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
